= Introduction <introduction>

While most #ndbd events in the CUORE detector are contained within a single crystal, approximately 5% deposit energy across two. This analysis searches for #ndbd decay in these dual-site events. We compare predicted background and simulated signal spectra with observed data to constrain the #ndbd decay half-life. Expected background components are derived from the CUORE Background Model (BM), using data and simulations processed according to the 1 ton-yr BM analysis. Unlike the BM analysis, however, we examine a limited energy range in 2D space. This results in lower coincident background and better relative sensitivity compared to the main single-site analysis.

The inputs for the fit, the data used and simulations are discussed in the next two chapters, and the Bayesian markov chain monte carlo method that is used to construct the posterior distribution for the #ndbd decay half life is presented in the section 4. The results and the systematics studies are discussed in the last two sections of this note.